---
source: crates/pipdock-cli/tests/golden.rs
expression: "stdout_of(&[cmd, \"--help\"])"
---
Update packages

Usage: pipdock update [OPTIONS] [PKGS]...

Arguments:
  [PKGS]...
          Packages to update; omit and pass `--all` for everything

Options:
      --all
          Update every outdated package (pins still apply)

      --env <PATH>
          Interpreter or environment directory. Defaults to the last used env, else an auto-detected `.venv` in the working directory

      --engine <ENGINE>
          Override the configured engine for this invocation

          Possible values:
          - pip: `<python> -m pip`
          - uv:  `uv pip --python <python>`

      --strategy <STRATEGY>
          Conflict strategy

          Possible values:
          - compatible: Accept the resolver's compatible version. The safe default
          - latest:     Force the latest version. Off a TTY this requires an explicit acknowledgement
          
          [default: compatible]

      --except <PKG,...>
          Ad-hoc exclusions on top of the pin list

      --json
          Machine-readable output; NDJSON for streaming commands

      --dry-run
          Print the resolution report and exit without changing anything

  -y, --yes
          Assume defaults on all prompts. Conflicts resolve to *skip*, never *force*

      --quiet
          Reduce log output

      --verbose
          Increase log output

      --log-file <PATH>
          Tee logs to a file

      --no-snapshot
          DANGEROUS: skip the pre-batch snapshot. CI images only; prints a warning.
          
          This is the sole documented escape from DATA-FLOW §9.2, and it exists because a throwaway CI container has nothing to roll back to.

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
